# Witness rows for the third-commutator flag in J₄

The rows of `basisRows` are a candidate row basis B, and `inverseRows`
is its candidate inverse. `tripleRows` lists the ten candidate matrices
B [gₖ,[gᵢ,gⱼ]] B⁻¹ in the order specified in `Words.lean`.
All rows use bit j for column j. These definitions assert no matrix identity.
The inverse is certified in `Basis.lean`; word realization and the linear
commutation implications have separate certificate obligations.

Source context: Aschbacher–Smith, Proposition 1.3.4, printed p.511
(PDF p.528 of `refs/quasithin.pdf`), and the ATLAS J₄ matrices in
`Theory/SpecificGroups/Janko4/Model/Data.lean`.
Reproduction: `CommutantFlag/source/generate.py`; witness data are untrusted.
-/

